<div class="audit-note"><h3>How to read this report</h3>
<p><strong>Scope:</strong> {{ $remainingOnly ? 'Loans and payroll obligations with a remaining balance at cutoff, and payroll periods ended' : 'All recorded loans, including settled loans, and payroll periods ended' }} on or before {{ $report['periodEnd'] }}. Approved and completed payrolls are included; completion does not mean salaries or authorities have been paid. Full monthly payroll amounts are used, with no daily proration. Figures cover loans and payroll only, rather than all trade or other company liabilities.</p>
<p><strong>Loan principal and interest:</strong> Each reference includes the saved loan code and internal record ID (#) to distinguish separate loans that share a code. Both loan display types are treated consistently here. Principal and interest are separate. A loan mentioned in another loan’s description is a relationship, not a repayment. Original principal is the gross contractual amount, which may differ from cash received when interest is withheld.</p>
<p><strong>Salary and statutory balances:</strong> Salaries are net amounts after deductions. EPF includes employee and employer contributions; ETF is the employer contribution; APIT is the recorded payroll tax deduction. These are separate payables, so employee EPF and tax are not added back to net salary. Preparing or submitting statutory documents does not clear a payment balance.</p>
<p><strong>Basis and limitations:</strong> This is a management schedule from current source records and dated settlements, not a locked historical ledger or an auditor’s certification. Later source edits, deleted payments and undated waivers can affect historical results. Interest is based on recorded due dates, not a daily accrual calculation. Draft imports and missing months require review; absent payment/submission records do not prove that no payment/submission happened outside this system. No penalties or unrecorded accruals are estimated.</p>
</div>
</section>
